{"toolCallId":"call_65ddc2f9934f4147bb88390a86773ea4","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"3:description: \"calculate-completeness.sh reports a completion percentage but always exits 0, so every caller has to scrape stdout to decide whether a packet passes. This adds an opt-in --min-percent <N> threshold that turns the report into an exit status without changing the report itself.\"\n39:Let a caller ask the question directly: run the script with `--min-percent <N>` and read the verdict from the exit status, while every existing caller keeps the exact report and the exact exit status it gets today.\n49:- A `--min-percent <N>` option in the script's argument parser, accepting an integer from 0 to 100.\n80:| REQ-001 | The parser accepts `--min-percent <N>` and consumes the next argument, leaving the positional `SPEC_FOLDER` and the existing `--file` path intact. | `--min-percent 90 <folder>` and `<folder> --min-percent 90` both parse to the same target and threshold. |\n81:| REQ-002 | When `--min-percent <N>` is supplied, the script exits `3` if the reported Overall Completion is below `N`, and exits `0` if it is equal to or above `N`. | A packet reporting 50% exits 3 at `--min-percent 90`, and 0 at `--min-percent 50` and `--min-percent 40`. |\n91:| REQ-007 | `--help` documents `--min-percent <N>` alongside the other options, including that it exits 3 below the threshold. | `--help` output contains one entry for the option; the rest of the help text is untouched. |\n93:| REQ-009 | In `--file` mode the report has no Overall Completion line, so the threshold compares against the single-file `Completion: N%` the script already prints. | `--file <path> --min-percent 90` exits 3 below 90 and 0 at or above it. |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"53a654","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
